{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c43f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07331-7853-7a51-8c8d-7bc0bf66c506"},"sequence":122,"recorded_at":1780531400000239,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0c99dc94-835c-41a8-b7dc-1156d61e2988","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0c99dc94-835c-41a8-b7dc-1156d61e2988","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0c99dc94-835c-41a8-b7dc-1156d61e2988"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"ca6c3bd2-9e0d-4aa0-9c58-4811aa8a00fd"},"task_id":"ca6c3bd2-9e0d-4aa0-9c58-4811aa8a00fd","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"ca6c3bd2-9e0d-4aa0-9c58-4811aa8a00fd","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-5-1\",\n  \"command\": \"tail -60 LOGBOOK.md; echo ===; git log --oneline -1; git status --short | head -20\",\n  \"description\": \"Inspect logbook tail and git state\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"- EVIDENCE: Each mutant grep-anchored (count==1), vet-checked, reverted byte-identical. H1 and H2 fail with `error = <nil>` (admission, no slide); H3 fails arm-blind at `document members`, as predicted — still fail-closed, now arm-pinned. Full `go test ./...` green, package coverage 88.6% -> 88.9%.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1snnef: terminal conformance harness and derived refusal-arm inventory\\n- FINDING: Deriving the refusal arms before writing the inventory found two genuinely unwitnessed arms, not review hypotheticals: `Registry.AdmitProbe` on a nil registry (nil check first, so no fixture needed) and `ParseEvidence` on malformed `observed_at`/`expires_at` (timestamp parse precedes identity recomputation, proven by the new cases passing). Both now have tests. Seven further arms are dead by construction with the bound stated, not inferred: two `evidence canonical bytes` arms (serializes a fixed string/bool/null map; `encoding/json` and JCS cannot fail on it) and five re-parse `document timestamp` arms after an already-validated member (this leaf's three plus `checkEvidenceLiveness`'s two, pinned as exactly these five).\\n- FINDING: The single dynamic-detail funnel is `Registration.validate` wrapping `validatePlatforms` via `err.Error()`. The inventory pins the funneled set exactly (three details, derived from the AST both ways) and allowlists plain-error construction to `validatePlatforms` and `DigestFile` only, with `DigestFile` failures asserted never-`*Error` behaviorally. A second funnel or a new plain-error refusal site is a red.\\n- DECISION: Row resolution is detail-mention OR (entry-mention AND wire-or-verified-predicate-mention), with predicates verified from the production AST. External tests assert codes through predicates with isolating fixtures; demanding detail strings there would misdescribe the battery. Misattribution (right detail, wrong test) remains a review finding — three such rows were caught by reading the generated table, not by the gate.\\n- EVIDENCE: 8 copy-aside mutants, each grep-confirmed present and restored `cmp`-clean: M1 replays the reviewer's exact attack (new arm, new detail) and fails forward naming the arm plus reverse on the count; M2 reuses an existing detail in a new function and fails on the function key; M3/M4/M7 narrow rather than delete and fail at `error = <nil>`; M5 (deleted relay refusal) fails the gate and both inventory directions via the stale row; M6 (swapped legacy map) fails three translation tests; M9 (deleted table row) fails forward plus the bijection. 8/8 killed, 0 survivors.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/conformance.go`, `conformance_test.go`, `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (new); `manifest_test.go` (+2 evidence-timestamp cases), `terminalbackend_test.go` (+5 wire codes); `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json` (+`terminal-lifecycle-conformance` acceptance case, 75->76), `traceability.go` (projection digest), `traceability_test.go`, `cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go`, `README.md`. Section bindings untouched: still `unevidenced` with honest gaps, no clause-level claims added.\\n- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14 packages), `-race` exit 0 (14 packages), `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0. Package coverage 89.9% statements (reviewer-measured on the rev-1 tree; 90.0% was my rounding error). New files left untracked in the working tree; no commit (board checkpoints). TASK-260830-1snnef handed to review.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1snnef round-1 rework: four sampled closures, closed by derivation\\n- FINDING (F1): The refusal-arm derivation walked FuncDecl bodies only, so a package-level `var f = func() *Error {…}` arm and an aliased constructor (`refuse := mismatchf`) each shipped reachable with a new detail while both inventory tests stayed green. Both shapes measured empty in the tree, so the 193/193 ratio held while the closure claim did not.\\n- FIX (F1, preferred over a caveat): the derivation now scans every FuncDecl body plus every package-level var initializer (attributed to the variable name), and `rejectConstructorAliases` fatals on any constructor reference outside direct-call position. Replayed both reviewer probes copy-aside with shasum-verified restore: A1 fails the bijection (194 derived vs 193 rows), A2 fatals at the alias. Zero table change — both shapes are still empty in the tree.\\n- FIX (F2): `TestCheckErrorAllowedRefusesEveryUnlistedCode` was a 3–5-code sample named as a complement. It now derives the complement: a full-row mirror table (`allowedErrorCodesByOperation`, all ten rows exact) is proved a subset of production by the exhaustive admit test and production is proved a subset of the mirror over the pinned catalog (`catalog.Current().Errors`) by the refusal loop, with a mirror-inside-catalog pin and fail-closed empty-domain guards. P20 (admit `terminal_backend_unavailable` for all ten ops) now fails the suite. Non-catalog strings are an unbounded domain: three probes pin the shape with the sampling bound stated, not claimed as closure.\\n- FIX (F3): added `CheckAttachResult(false, false, auth{InputAuthorized:true})` — the case only the third conjunct catches. Dropping `resultInputAuthorized != auth.InputAuthorized` now fails the suite.\\n- FIX (F4): attach expiry pinned from both sides — admitted one second before `expires`, refused exactly at it. `!now.Before(expires)` → `now.After(expires)` now fails the suite.\\n- BOUNDS (carried forward, not dropped): the inventory kills every arm-deleting mutant by construction, so post-leaf-3 mutation scores are NOT comparable to leaf 2's 91/95 — stated in the inventory file's Stated bounds block and here. Attribution drift survives via the entry+code fallback — live example `CheckTransition`'s dead `\\\"operation vocabulary\\\"` arm resolving through `ParseOperation`'s test — also stated there. Declined closure: P13 (empty-ID `ProjectToLegacy` still refuses, different wire code). P11 (legacy escape name) is no longer declined: C20 (`legacyForward` gains `\\\"screen\\\"`) is killed by `TestLegacyReverseProjectionExistsOnlyForThePair`, so the closed-set property is pinned.\\n- EVIDENCE: A1/A2/P8/P16/P20 replayed, each red with exit 1, tree restored byte-identical (shasum). Full gates re-run below.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (derivation + bounds), `conformance_test.go` (F2–F4); `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry, 89.9% correction). No production change, no table change, README sentence stands as written now that the derivation covers it.\\n- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14/14), `-race` on terminalbackend exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (`acceptance_cases=76`, section coverage unchanged). Package coverage 90.0% statements measured on this rework tree (test-only additions vs the rev-1 tree the reviewer measured at 89.9%). Rework left uncommitted in the working tree per the brief (board checkpoints, no commit).\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1snnef round-2 rework: three sampled closures of one family, closed by derivation\\n- FINDING (G2): `TestPlainErrorsLiveOnlyInTheirTwoFunctions` walked FuncDecl bodies only — the exact walk `deriveRefusalArms` was extended past in round 1, 200 lines above in the same file. Identical `errors.New` text was red in a FuncDecl and green in a package-level var (W5b), `fmt.Errorf` likewise (W9b), var func literal likewise (W16).\\n- FIX (G2): the sibling walk gained the same GenDecl/ValueSpec loop (shared `isPlainErrorConstruction` helper, receiver-qualified method names). Twin-hunt over the story boundary (`internal/terminalbackend` AST walks): `deriveRefusalArms` already extended, `rejectConstructorAliases` inspects whole files, `productionCodeSymbols` walks package-level const GenDecls by construction, `testBodies`/`predicateCodes` are func-scoped by convention and fail closed, the platform funnel is function-scoped by design. No other twin. Bonus kill: an unused package-level plain-error var (W18 shape) is now red too — its initializer runs at package init, so the construction is real.\\n- FIX (G1): `TestCheckStatusResultEnforcesLookupRules` now derives the complement — every state the production parser admits (`derivedParserVocabulary` over the switch-case list) outside parked/active is refused with attach evidenced; parked/active admitted. C13/C26/C27/C28/C29 each red, C30 still red.\\n- FIX (G3): new internal `TestReplicationMembersAreExactlyTheClosedTable` pins the live `replicationMembers` map in both directions plus the size (64 members). C40c (add) and C40-init-injection red there; C40b/C40d red there and at the entry. External test comment restated to its half (want subset production) with the reverse cited.\\n- FIX (G4): new `TestDerivedVocabulariesAreExactlyTheAdmittedSets` derives all four parser vocabularies (states, operations, effects, transports) from switch-case lists resolved through string consts, both directions plus size, and pins `conformanceOperations` to the derived operation set — the \\\"pinned by\\\" citation now holds. Refused samples restated as sampling bounds over the unbounded string domain and extended with the reviewer's exact survivor strings (`detached`, `detach`, `input_reopened`, `ssh_tunnel`), each now behaviorally refused.\\n- BOUNDS (recorded, not closed): W11 (DigestFile allowlist is function-wide, no detail pin), W13 (bespoke error types outside both spellings), mismatchf format-verb interpolation (derivation now fatals on any constructor call without exactly one string-literal argument — zero such sites today; vet catches non-constant formats). P11 stale bound dropped (C20 killed); P13 declined closure stands.\\n- TOOLING: round-3 runner (`.temp/TASK-260830-1snnef-r2/probe.py` family successor `.temp/TASK-260830-1snnef-r3/probe3.py`) snapshots and hash-verifies every touched file regardless of extension, with a JSON-restore self-test and a porcelain+fingerprint tree-identity check — a T01-shaped JSON mutation can no longer contaminate the tree.\\n- EVIDENCE: 21/21 replayed red, 0 survived, 0 anchor-missing (G1x6 incl. control, G2x5 incl. control and unused-var, G3x4 incl. init injection and both reclassifications, G4x5 incl. control, F2 guard). Tree verified identical before/after (porcelain + watched hashes).\\n- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/conformance_test.go` (G1/G3-comment/G4), `internal_pin_test.go` (G3 pin), `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (G2 twin + single-arg assertion + bounds), `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry + P11 correction). No production change, no arm-table change, 193/193 undisturbed.\\n- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14/14), `-race` on terminalbackend exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (`acceptance_cases=76`, `clauses_discharged=17/403`). Package coverage 90.0% statements. Rework left uncommitted in the working tree per the brief (board checkpoints, no commit).\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1snnef round-3 rework: unpinned legacyForward closed by a white-box pin, plus a correction\\n- CORRECTION: the round-1 and round-2 entries above claim C20 (`legacyForward` gains `\\\"screen\\\"`) is killed by `TestLegacyReverseProjectionExistsOnlyForThePair` and drop the P11 bound on that basis. That claim is false, and the error is the reviewer's (round-2 verdict), not the producer's — the rework followed the verdict. C20 lands on `BuiltinTmux` while `ProjectToLegacy` iterates a map, so the kill was a coin flip over iteration order: 5 red and 7 green across 12 runs of the reviewer's own probe. A single red on a map-iteration mutant proves nothing. LESSON, applied to every mutant below: a mutant over map iteration (or anything else iterating a map, e.g. `ProjectToLegacy`) is run repeatedly before its verdict is believed.\\n- FIX (H1, blocking): new white-box `TestLegacyForwardIsExactlyTheImmutablePair` (`internal_pin_test.go`) holds the live `legacyForward` map to exactly `{tmux, conpty}` in both directions plus the size — the `replicationMembers` idiom from this same CR — and additionally pins injectivity (distinct canonical values), which `ProjectToLegacy`'s documented determinism rested on unenforced. The black-box forward comment is restated to its half (sampling bound, not closure) with the reverse cited, and the reviewer's escape strings join the refused samples (`TranslateLegacyBackend(\\\"screen\\\")`, `ProjectToLegacy(\\\"vendor.screen\\\")`).\\n- FIX (H2, bound, closed cheaply): new `rejectPlainErrorAliases` fails the suite on any `errors.New`/`fmt.Errorf`-kin reference outside direct-call position, in every function including the two allowlisted ones (an alias inside `validatePlatforms` would bypass the funneled detail pin). Stated bounds and the allowlist test comment record the closure. Bespoke error types outside both spellings remain the disclosed bound.\\n- EVIDENCE: L3 (`\\\"screen\\\": \\\"vendor.screen\\\"`) 12/12 red, C20 (`\\\"screen\\\": BuiltinTmux`) 12/12 red, each over `-run TestLegacy|TestHistorical`; the new pin alone red on C20 with the size message (`holds 3 names, want exactly 2`); H2 alias (`var newPlain = errors.New` + call from a FuncDecl) 3/3 red on `TestPlainErrors`. Tree verified identical before/after (file-content compare + restore assert).\\n- SCOPE: `internal/terminalbackend/internal_pin_test.go` (H1 pin), `conformance_test.go` (H1 comment + 2 samples), `refusal_arm_inventory_test.go` (H2 alias gate + bounds), `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry). No production change, no arm-table change, 193/193 undisturbed.\\n- STATUS: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (14/14), `-race` on terminalbackend exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (`acceptance_cases=76`, `clauses_discharged=17/403`). Rework left uncommitted in the working tree per the brief (board checkpoints, no commit).\\n\\n### 2321 — A local copy of a shared gate needs a pin, not a comment; a registry that only counts itself cannot see new code\\n- ROOT CAUSE (B3): `provhost.decodeStrictObject` re-implemented strict decoding without the shared `canonicaljson` surrogate rule, and Go's `encoding/json` replaces a lone `\\\\ud800` escape with U+FFFD silently — so Section 1.6 wire bodies carrying lone surrogates were admitted. Same class as the sibling story's decoder gap.\\n- FIX: local `hasLoneSurrogateEscape` gate in `internal/provhost/surrogate.go` (local copy because `canonicaljson` is frozen across both unlanded stories), called first from `decodeStrictObject`; one `\\\\ud800` fixture per production entry plus `TestSurrogateGateAgreesWithCanonicalJSON`, a 13-vector pin driving both the local gate and `canonicaljson.Canonicalize` so the copies cannot drift.\\n- ANOMALY: the first gate version used `switch` and reddened `TestAllProductionSwitchesAreClassified` — the package census bans switches as membership-gate hiding spots. Rewritten with if/else, identical verdicts, green. A gate's own residue rules apply to the fix too.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (B4): `tracecheck` verifies registry -> code only, so ~3,700 lines of `internal/provider` + `internal/provhost` landed with the gate green under gap prose asserting \\\"no provider manifest is implemented anywhere\\\". The census enumerates what registered itself.\\n- FIX: 4 acceptance cases + 4 section bindings (7.1, 7.6, 7.7, 8), 4 gap rewrites (5.5, 7.2, 7.3, 7.5), re-pinned hash; report now bindings=53 unevidenced=45 clauses 17/428. Reverse scan (every `internal/*` package owned or explicitly excluded) recorded as open work, not implemented here.\\n- DECISION (A2/A3/A4, recorded in code): CheckIdentity duplication is deliberate (different error surface, shared package frozen); Provider Protocol 3.0.0 is a stated non-owner bound, not a defect; provider's cause-appending errors must be rebuilt, not quoted, at the future cmd/ax lift (`refuseCausalLeak`).\\n- SCOPE: `internal/provhost/surrogate*.go`, `protocol.go`, refusal inventory (floor 162->164), `profile_test.go` (cross-plane set test), `identity.go`/`doc.go` bounds, `internal/provider/doc.go` composition contract, ownership registry + pin + report/golden/README figures.\\n- STATUS: Resolved. `go test ./...` and `-cover` green, vet + GOOS=windows vet + gofmt clean, admit-all and narrowing mutants red as required. TASK-260830-32jeti round-4, handed to review.\\n\\n### 1244 — A deadline borrowed from pipe ownership is not a deadline; a shared hand list is not a pin\\n- ROOT CAUSE (F1): the `os.Pipe` rewrite in `internal/provhost/runner.go` fixed the Wait-closes-StdoutPipe race but removed the only thing that unblocked the post-Wait drain. `exec.WaitDelay` closes pipes exec itself owns; with caller-supplied `*os.File` pipes nothing closes them, so `readCapped` waits for EOF until every writer is gone and a setsid-detached grandchild holds `Host.Call` open for its whole lifetime (measured 20.3-20.7s against sleep 20, frame accepted with err=nil).\\n- FIX: the waiter owns the bound now — `command.Wait()` runs in a goroutine under `select` on the call context, both drains collect through `collectDrains` under the same context, and closing the read ends fails blocked drains at once. A `Process.Kill` backstop covers a self-detached direct child, which the group-aimed `Cancel` misses. The round-6 EPIPE rule is untouched: with the wait reaped and stdout holding a frame, the frame still governs.\\n- ANOMALY: the first regression probe passed vacuously in 0.79s — python3 cold start under load can exceed the 400ms deadline kill, so no grandchild ever existed to hold the pipe. A hang test whose fixture loses a startup race proves nothing. Rebuilt on perl (millisecond start) with the kill seconds away; 3/3 red at the sleeper lifetime before the fix, green at the deadline after.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (F2): the 13-vector corpus was literal-versus-literal — both implementations matched the same hand list, so a narrowed low-surrogate ceiling (SG1, 1023 admitted) and a narrowed uppercase hex range (SG5, 473 admitted) survived 6/6. Raw WTF-8 (`\\\\xed\\\\xa0\\\\x80`) arrived through an encoding the escape scanner never sees and became U+FFFD silently.\\n- FIX: `decodeStrictObject` refuses non-UTF-8 first (mirroring `canonicaljson.decodeStrict` order), and the corpus is replaced by a 239,630-vector derived sweep — full BMP x hex case, surrogate x 16 case mixes, high x boundary/non-low seconds, sampled positions plus all-surrogate member names, full BMP raw (WTF-8 form for surrogates), malformed patterns, astral samples — every verdict judged by the independent implementation. SG1 diverges on 19,482 vectors, SG5 on 4,411; gate removal reddens the identity row with err=nil and the sweep on 2,059.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (F3): `checkResponseMembers` ran before the version gate, so only a v2-shaped 3.x envelope reached `incompatible_protocol`; the tree's own pinned 7.2 quote scopes that member rule to major 2. Fixed the ordering, not the doc: a `foreignMajor` peek (protocol identity plus readable foreign version, trusts nothing, refuses nothing) skips the v2 `ok`/member rules so the single existing mismatch site decides. No new refusal arm; floor untouched by F3.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/provhost/runner.go`, `protocol.go`, `surrogate*.go`, `identity.go` + comment corrections, `runner_test.go`, `protocol_test.go`, `identity_test.go`, refusal inventory (floor 164->166: one UTF-8 frame arm plus its status-body expansion, each witnessed).\\n- STATUS: Resolved. Build, vet, GOOS=windows vet, gofmt clean; `go test ./...` 15/15 green; provhost `-race` green; provhost 85.8%, provider 97.0%. TASK-260830-32jeti round-8, handed to review.\\n===\\n2512f20 Record STORY-260830-3m2mw8 board state\\n M .github/workflows/ci.yml\\n M LOGBOOK.md\\n M README.md\\n M internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go\\n M internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json\\n M internal/traceability/traceability.go\\n M internal/traceability/traceability_test.go\\n?? internal/provhost/\\n?? internal/provider/\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 19775,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 4944,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
