{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5cb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07331-7853-7a51-8c8d-7bc0bf66c506"},"sequence":320,"recorded_at":1780531400000635,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0c99dc94-835c-41a8-b7dc-1156d61e2988","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0c99dc94-835c-41a8-b7dc-1156d61e2988","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0c99dc94-835c-41a8-b7dc-1156d61e2988"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"cc0238be-f5ee-43bd-aef9-859ae352c07d"},"task_id":"cc0238be-f5ee-43bd-aef9-859ae352c07d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"cc0238be-f5ee-43bd-aef9-859ae352c07d","chunk":"Read text file `LOGBOOK.md`.\n(884 line(s) above)\n885|\n886|### 1244 — A deadline borrowed from pipe ownership is not a deadline; a shared hand list is not a pin\n887|- ROOT CAUSE (F1): the `os.Pipe` rewrite in `internal/provhost/runner.go` fixed the Wait-closes-StdoutPipe race but removed the only thing that unblocked the post-Wait drain. `exec.WaitDelay` closes pipes exec itself owns; with caller-supplied `*os.File` pipes nothing closes them, so `readCapped` waits for EOF until every writer is gone and a setsid-detached grandchild holds `Host.Call` open for its whole lifetime (measured 20.3-20.7s against sleep 20, frame accepted with err=nil).\n888|- FIX: the waiter owns the bound now — `command.Wait()` runs in a goroutine under `select` on the call context, both drains collect through `collectDrains` under the same context, and closing the read ends fails blocked drains at once. A `Process.Kill` backstop covers a self-detached direct child, which the group-aimed `Cancel` misses. The round-6 EPIPE rule is untouched: with the wait reaped and stdout holding a frame, the frame still governs.\n889|- ANOMALY: the first regression probe passed vacuously in 0.79s — python3 cold start under load can exceed the 400ms deadline kill, so no grandchild ever existed to hold the pipe. A hang test whose fixture loses a startup race proves nothing. Rebuilt on perl (millisecond start) with the kill seconds away; 3/3 red at the sleeper lifetime before the fix, green at the deadline after.\n890|- ROOT CAUSE (F2): the 13-vector corpus was literal-versus-literal — both implementations matched the same hand list, so a narrowed low-surrogate ceiling (SG1, 1023 admitted) and a narrowed uppercase hex range (SG5, 473 admitted) survived 6/6. Raw WTF-8 (`\\xed\\xa0\\x80`) arrived through an encoding the escape scanner never sees and became U+FFFD silently.\n891|- FIX: `decodeStrictObject` refuses non-UTF-8 first (mirroring `canonicaljson.decodeStrict` order), and the corpus is replaced by a 239,630-vector derived sweep — full BMP x hex case, surrogate x 16 case mixes, high x boundary/non-low seconds, sampled positions plus all-surrogate member names, full BMP raw (WTF-8 form for surrogates), malformed patterns, astral samples — every verdict judged by the independent implementation. SG1 diverges on 19,482 vectors, SG5 on 4,411; gate removal reddens the identity row with err=nil and the sweep on 2,059.\n892|- ROOT CAUSE (F3): `checkResponseMembers` ran before the version gate, so only a v2-shaped 3.x envelope reached `incompatible_protocol`; the tree's own pinned 7.2 quote scopes that member rule to major 2. Fixed the ordering, not the doc: a `foreignMajor` peek (protocol identity plus readable foreign version, trusts nothing, refuses nothing) skips the v2 `ok`/member rules so the single existing mismatch site decides. No new refusal arm; floor untouched by F3.\n893|- SCOPE: `internal/provhost/runner.go`, `protocol.go`, `surrogate*.go`, `identity.go` + comment corrections, `runner_test.go`, `protocol_test.go`, `identity_test.go`, refusal inventory (floor 164->166: one UTF-8 frame arm plus its status-body expansion, each witnessed).\n894|- STATUS: Resolved. Build, vet, GOOS=windows vet, gofmt clean; `go test ./...` 15/15 green; provhost `-race` green; provhost 85.8%, provider 97.0%. TASK-260830-32jeti round-8, handed to review."}}}
