{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5ef","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07331-7853-7a51-8c8d-7bc0bf66c506"},"sequence":338,"recorded_at":1780531400000671,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0c99dc94-835c-41a8-b7dc-1156d61e2988","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0c99dc94-835c-41a8-b7dc-1156d61e2988","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0c99dc94-835c-41a8-b7dc-1156d61e2988"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"7f4c95cd-45ed-4ec1-9f33-0d4c17d568b1"},"task_id":"7f4c95cd-45ed-4ec1-9f33-0d4c17d568b1","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"7f4c95cd-45ed-4ec1-9f33-0d4c17d568b1","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: line 894\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-- STATUS: Resolved. Build, vet, GOOS=windows vet, gofmt clean; `go test ./...` 15/15 green; provhost `-race` green; provhost 85.8%, provider 97.0%. TASK-260830-32jeti round-8, handed to review.\n+- STATUS: Resolved. Build, vet, GOOS=windows vet, gofmt clean; `go test ./...` 15/15 green; provhost `-race` green; provhost 85.8%, provider 97.0%. TASK-260830-32jeti round-8, handed to review.\n+\n+### TASK-260830-32jeti: two green branches, one red combination — syscall.Mkfifo under GOOS=windows vet\n+- FINDING: the new CI step `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` failed on the merged tree with `terminalbackend_test.go:972:20: undefined: syscall.Mkfifo` — the only failure across all 16 packages. Invisible on both parents by construction: the story branch added the gate before the package existed (nothing to compile, exit 0), and trunk added the `syscall.Mkfifo` FIFO case without the gate (never compiled under Windows). Each branch was green on its own; only the combination is red. A per-branch gate that never meets the code it must check proves nothing about the merge.\n+- FIX: moved only the FIFO case out of `TestDigestFile` into `TestDigestFileRefusesFIFO` in new `internal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend_unix_test.go`, following the `internal/localstore/projection_unix_test.go` pattern. Correction worth recording: the `_unix` filename suffix alone constrains nothing (`unix` is a build tag, not a GOOS value, so the suffix form matches no `_GOOS` pattern) — the first attempt with suffix-only still failed windows vet, and the explicit `//go:build unix` line is what excludes Windows. The shared test file drops the `syscall` import and keeps a pointer comment; no other Go file touched.\n+- EVIDENCE: `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` exit 0, `go vet ./...` exit 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./... -count=1` 16/16 green with `TestDigestFileRefusesFIFO` observed PASS on linux (a moved test that stops executing is not a fix), `tracecheck` exit 0. TASK-260830-32jeti, handed to review.\n"}}}
