{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c72b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07331-7853-7a51-8c8d-7bc0bf66c506"},"sequence":496,"recorded_at":1780531400000987,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0c99dc94-835c-41a8-b7dc-1156d61e2988","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"0c99dc94-835c-41a8-b7dc-1156d61e2988","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0c99dc94-835c-41a8-b7dc-1156d61e2988"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Fix handed off to review.\n\nWhat was wrong: `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` failed with one error — `terminalbackend_test.go:972: undefined: syscall.Mkfifo`. Two green parents, one red merge: the gate branch had no package to compile, trunk had no gate to compile under.\n\nFix (nothing else touched): moved only the FIFO assertions from `TestDigestFile` into new `TestDigestFileRefusesFIFO` in `internal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend_unix_test.go`, following the `projection_unix_test.go` pattern; dropped the `syscall` import from the shared file. One correction found along the way: the `_unix` suffix alone does not exclude Windows (`unix` is a build tag, not a GOOS), so the file also carries an explicit `//go:build unix` — verified when the suffix-only attempt still failed vet.\n\nEvidence, all run directly: Windows vet exit 0, Linux vet exit 0, gofmt clean, full suite 16/16 green with the moved test observed PASS on Linux, tracecheck exit 0. Details attached as `TASK-260830-32jeti_verification-evidence.md`, plus a `LOGBOOK.md` entry. Per the brief nothing was committed or pushed; the worktree HEAD is `2512f20` and the delta is the two test files plus the logbook entry.","reason":null}}
